<% content_for :title, "Made to order" %>
<%= render "shared/page_hero", eyebrow: "Custom work", title: "Made to order", lede: "Some of what we print is never listed. If you can describe it, ask." %>
<div class="page"><div class="wrap two">
  <div class="prose">
    <h2>What you can ask for</h2>
    <ul>
      <li><b>Coasters</b> with a name, a date, a quote or a logo, for a home, a wedding, an event or a business.</li>
      <li><b>Team and club coasters</b> with your logo set into the center, in your colors. Teams ask for these most.</li>
      <li><b>Desk signs, plaques and name tags</b> for an office or a front desk.</li>
      <li><b>Watch stands</b> with your own text on the base.</li>
      <li><b>Spiral pen holders</b> on a round base with a name on it, for any person, company or organization, in colors you choose. A good gift for a desk, a new hire or a client.</li>
      <li><b>Gifts for a team or a client,</b> in your colors, in the quantity you need.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2>A spiral pen holder</h2>
    <div class="photo-pair two-up">
      <%= image_tag "photos/spiral-pen-holder-2298.jpg", alt: "An orange spiral pen holder on a wooden table, seen from the side", loading: "lazy" %>
      <%= image_tag "photos/spiral-pen-holder-2300.jpg", alt: "The same orange spiral pen holder from a slightly different angle", loading: "lazy" %>
    </div>
    <p>A twisted cup in the color you choose, standing on a round base with a name on it. We make them for a person, a company or an organization, in sizes from about 2 inches to 6 inches tall. The same spiral also makes a toothbrush holder, about 4 inches tall, with a hole in the bottom so water can drain out.</p>
    <h2>A phone and watch holder</h2>
    <div class="photo-pair two-up wide">
      <%= image_tag "photos/dual-holder-front.jpg", alt: "A blue dual holder on an oval base, two upright stands side by side", loading: "lazy" %>
      <%= image_tag "photos/dual-holder-angle.jpg", alt: "The same blue dual holder seen from the side", loading: "lazy" %>
    </div>
    <p>Two stands side by side on one oval base, made for a phone and a watch, in the color you choose. It also works as a small jewelry holder, for a watch and for bracelets and bangles.</p>
    <h2>A tall watch stand with two brackets</h2>
    <div class="photo-pair two-up wide">
      <%= image_tag "photos/tall-stand-blue-front.jpg", alt: "A light blue watch stand on a round base with two brackets stacked on the column and text on the base", loading: "lazy" %>
      <%= image_tag "photos/tall-stand-blue-side.jpg", alt: "The same light blue stand seen from the side, showing the two brackets", loading: "lazy" %>
    </div>
    <p>Two brackets stacked on one column, standing on a round base with your own text. Shown here in light blue.</p>
    <h2>Gingerbread figures for the holidays</h2>
    <div class="photo-pair two-up">
      <%= image_tag "photos/gingerbread-magnets-fridge-wide.jpg", alt: "Three gingerbread magnets on a stainless steel refrigerator door, one smiling, one surprised and one cross", loading: "lazy" %>
      <%= image_tag "photos/gingerbread-magnets-fridge-tall.jpg", alt: "Three gingerbread magnets stacked down the side of a refrigerator door", loading: "lazy" %>
    </div>
    <p>We designed these for the holidays: dark brown gingerbread figures with white icing lines and red and green buttons, each with its own face, made as magnets for the refrigerator, shown here, and as tree ornaments. Ask us if you would like a set.</p>
    <h2>How long it takes</h2>
    <p>Up to four coasters usually ship in 3 to 4 days, and within 7 days at the latest. A custom design adds design time, so tell us the date you need it.</p>
    <h2>How it works</h2>
    <ol>
      <li>Tell us what you have in mind: what it is, how many, and by when.</li>
      <li>Pick up to two colors and send us your text or your logo.</li>
      <li>We show you what it will look like before we print.</li>
      <li>We print it to order and send it.</li>
    </ol>
    <h2>Our colors</h2>
    <%= render "shared/palette" %>
    <p>Pick up to two. Most of our pieces are printed in PLA, and some in PETG. We can also print in ASA and in TPU. TPU is flexible, so a print can follow a curved surface, such as the body of a car. Tell us what the piece needs to do, because we pick the filament for the use. That is why we keep so many kinds, and a dryer for the filament. The right material depends on where the piece will live: the hitch cover on my Jeep is PLA, and the one on my father's is PETG, because we live in different temperature zones.</p>
  </div>
  <aside class="card" id="request">
    <% if params[:sent].present? %>
      <h3>Thank you</h3>
      <p>We have your request and will write back to you by email, usually within a day or two.</p>
    <% else %>
      <h3>Describe what you need</h3>
      <p>Tell us what it is, how many, and by when. We will write back with questions and a price before we print anything.</p>
      <% if @request&.errors&.any? %><p class="small"><b><%= @request.errors.full_messages.to_sentence %></b></p><% end %>
      <%= form_with model: @request, url: made_to_order_path, scope: :print_request, class: "request-form" do |f| %>
        <label>Your name<%= f.text_field :name, required: true, maxlength: 200, autocomplete: "name" %></label>
        <label>Your email<%= f.email_field :email, required: true, maxlength: 320, autocomplete: "email" %></label>
        <label>What would you like?<%= f.text_area :description, required: true, rows: 6, maxlength: 5000, placeholder: "For example: 12 team coasters with our logo in purple and gold" %></label>
        <label>How many?<%= f.text_field :quantity, maxlength: 200 %></label>
        <label>Needed by<%= f.text_field :needed_by, maxlength: 200, placeholder: "A date, or no rush" %></label>
        <div style="position:absolute;left:-9999px" aria-hidden="true"><label>Leave this empty<input type="text" name="website" tabindex="-1" autocomplete="off"></label></div>
        <%= f.submit "Send request", class: "btn" %>
      <% end %>
      <p class="small">Prefer email? Write to <a href="mailto:<%= Catalog::EMAIL %>?subject=Custom%20order"><%= Catalog::EMAIL %></a>, or use our <%= link_to "Etsy shop", Catalog::SHOP_URL, target: "_blank", rel: "noopener" %>. We use what you send only to answer your request.</p>
    <% end %>
  </aside>
</div></div>
